<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Alexander is a 32-year-old army commander with post-traumatic chest wall pain and a localized left fibrothorax after an old penetrating chest wound, a mild alcohol use disorder with a moderation goal, and bereavement, who comes for his preventive visit a week after his six-week review. His army is resting in the city and he expects to stay in the region through the summer, with field work in the river valleys and marshes and a further campaign planned. His chest pain is down to 3 of 10 and he is running again. He has kept to his drinking limits at all but one banquet. The forearm cut has healed and the sutures are out; he had Tdap at that visit. His military record shows a full childhood series, including MMR, polio and hepatitis B; he has never had hepatitis A or typhoid vaccines. He has never smoked. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Visit</td><td>Periodic adult preventive visit, age 32</td></tr><tr><td>Travel</td><td>Months in Mesopotamia (modern Iraq), in the field, with a campaign planned</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>Within his limits at all but one banquet; PEth 88 ng/mL a week ago</td></tr><tr><td>Mood</td><td>PHQ-2 1; PHQ-9 8 a week ago</td></tr><tr><td>Medicines</td><td>Lidocaine patch daily, thiamine 100 mg daily, acetaminophen as needed</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Health risk assessment. Completed by the patient on paper in the waiting room and reviewed with him by Dr. Papadakis-Mensah. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Domain</th><th>Finding</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Self-rated health</td><td>Good, and better than two months ago</td></tr><tr><td>Psychosocial</td><td>Grieving his companion; sees the behavioral health clinician every two weeks; heavy responsibility for his army</td></tr><tr><td>Alcohol</td><td>Moderation goal kept at all but one banquet; AUDIT 19 at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Physical activity</td><td>Trains daily; running again; physical therapy exercises most days</td></tr><tr><td>Nutrition</td><td>Irregular meals on the march; better in the city</td></tr><tr><td>Sleep</td><td>Six to seven hours</td></tr><tr><td>Safety</td><td>Service pistol in the armory off duty; does not ride or drive after drinking; wears a helmet and body armor in training</td></tr><tr><td>Activities of daily living</td><td>Independent</td></tr><tr><td>Hearing and vision</td><td>No problems; uses hearing protection on the firing range</td></tr><tr><td>Oral health</td><td>Dental check a year ago</td></tr><tr><td>Sexual health</td><td>No concerns raised; HIV and hepatitis screening offered and accepted</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

