<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.9" extension="2014-06-09"/>
    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Periodic adult preventive visit completed, with travel and campaign health</content>. Health risk assessment reviewed and the prevention plan updated for months in the field in Mesopotamia. CDC lists no malaria transmission in Iraq, so malaria chemoprophylaxis is not indicated; sandfly-borne leishmaniasis and tick-borne Crimean-Congo hemorrhagic fever are risks in the field. CDC recommends hepatitis A and typhoid vaccines for most travelers there. [S]<list><item>Hepatitis A (first dose) and typhoid Vi vaccines today; second hepatitis A dose in six to twelve months; typhoid booster in two years if exposure continues.</item><item>Insect and tick precautions: DEET or picaridin repellent, permethrin-treated uniforms, bed nets in the field, and checking for ticks; no handling of slaughtered animals without gloves.</item><item>Safe food and water; oral rehydration salts in his kit for diarrhea.</item><item>Malaria chemoprophylaxis to be reviewed before any travel to an area with transmission.</item><item>Rabies pre-exposure vaccination discussed; he declined for now and knows to seek care the same day after any animal bite.</item><item>HIV, hepatitis C and hepatitis B screening drawn today.</item><item>Influenza vaccine in the autumn; next preventive visit in one year.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder, mild (F10.10)</content>. Keeping to his moderation goal at all but one banquet. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; service pistol in the armory off duty; 988 card carried. [S]<list><item>Continue sessions with the addiction medicine clinician.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Personalized prevention plan. A written copy was given to the patient. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Service</th><th>Status</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Blood pressure</td><td>Completed today</td><td>122/78 mmHg</td></tr><tr><td>Lipid screening and cardiovascular risk</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>At 32 with no risk factors; statin assessment from 40</td></tr><tr><td>Diabetes screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>From 35 if overweight; BMI 24.7; fasting glucose 91 mg/dL at intake</td></tr><tr><td>Colorectal cancer screening</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>From 45</td></tr><tr><td>Tobacco use</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Never smoked</td></tr><tr><td>Unhealthy alcohol use</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Mild alcohol use disorder in care; moderation goal; PEth falling</td></tr><tr><td>Depression screening</td><td>Completed today</td><td>PHQ-2 1; grief followed with the PHQ-9</td></tr><tr><td>HIV screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis C screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Drawn today</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis B screening</td><td>Ordered</td><td>Triple panel drawn today; vaccinated in childhood</td></tr><tr><td>Tetanus, diphtheria, and pertussis</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Tdap three weeks ago for a wound</td></tr><tr><td>Measles, mumps, and rubella</td><td>Up to date</td><td>Two doses in childhood by his military record</td></tr><tr><td>Hepatitis A vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>First dose today for travel; second in six to twelve months</td></tr><tr><td>Typhoid vaccine</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Vi polysaccharide vaccine today for travel</td></tr><tr><td>Malaria prevention</td><td>Not indicated</td><td>CDC lists no malaria transmission in Iraq; review before travel to any area with transmission; bite precautions in any case</td></tr><tr><td>Insect and tick bite prevention</td><td>Completed today</td><td>Repellent, permethrin-treated uniforms, bed nets and tick checks for leishmaniasis and Crimean-Congo hemorrhagic fever</td></tr><tr><td>Rabies pre-exposure vaccination</td><td>Declined</td><td>Discussed for work with dogs and horses in the field; he declined for now; same-day care after any bite</td></tr><tr><td>Influenza vaccine</td><td>Due</td><td>In the autumn</td></tr><tr><td>COVID-19 vaccine</td><td>Up to date</td><td>This season&apos;s dose with his unit</td></tr><tr><td>Dental examination</td><td>Up to date</td><td>A year ago</td></tr></tbody></table><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Hepatitis A vaccine, adult, first of two doses, for travel; Typhoid Vi polysaccharide vaccine, one dose, for travel [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: Unhealthy Alcohol Use in Adolescents and Adults: Screening and Behavioral Counseling Interventions (2018); Medicare Preventive Services reference: visit templates, screening cascades, and documentation elements (2026); USPSTF A and B Recommendations (2026); Prevention of Hepatitis A Virus Infection in the United States: Recommendations of the Advisory Committee on Immunization Practices, 2020 (2020); Iraq: Traveler View (vaccines and medicines, and insect- and tick-borne disease) (2026); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Nine-week review in two weeks with repeat spirometry and PEth. The clinic or 988 at any hour. Next preventive visit in one year. Next scheduled visit 2026-05-11: nine-week review: repeat spirometry, pain, drinking and PEth, AUDIT-C, mood, safety and the plan ahead. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="2.16.840.1.113883.10.20.22.2.21" extension="2015-08-01"/>
    <code code="42348-3" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Advance directives"/>
    <title>Advance Care Planning</title>
    <text><paragraph>Voluntary advance care planning discussion of about 20 minutes, with his consent. Because his work carries a real risk of injury, he named a health care agent and completed a health care proxy form; the agent is recorded in the chart and is not named here. He said that what matters most to him is to lead his soldiers and to be fit to do it, and he asked that after a serious injury every reasonable treatment be tried. He chose not to record other treatment preferences now; the plan will be revisited at his next preventive visit. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>
